# Mutation Plan

The primary runner rejects 30 mutations spanning:

- stale authority and preregistration;
- commuting/deleted chirality, false M2 sufficiency, and broken matrix units;
- non-TP compression, cubic failure, and scalar probability lookup;
- wrong effects/roots, nonorthogonal Records, and incomplete writers;
- Record-typed conditions, occupied targets, nonlocal/simultaneous activity,
  overwrite, skipped bridge, and wrong eta;
- state reset, uncoupled successors, wrong sharp contrast, and host scheduling;
- arbitrary-history, rate, axiom, TOE, retention, and premature-H2 claims.

The independent runner rejects 24 separately named mutations using its direct
Kraus, C32-cylinder, set-geometry, and scope checks.  Every mutation must make
its runner exit nonzero; a changed label without a changed physical object is
not counted.
